,91],"tags","code-world-model","program-synthesis","model-based-planning","gridworld","NeurIPS-2024","Project source",[94],{"_51":92,"_25":95},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.12275","Why it belongs here","WorldCoder, a Model-Based LLM Agent represents knowledge of a world as executable Python programs. Interaction records constrain those programs, and planning searches for potential rewards. This NeurIPS 2024 work is primarily evaluated on gridworlds and task planning. It supports study of rule discovery and model repair rather than complete visual game generation.","detail","guidance","Resource type","Paper","Category","category","lead","summary","name","world","paper",[87,88,89,90,91],[114,115,107],[113,107],2024,"2d","plan","code",{"_117":118},"documents",{"_119":120,"_121":122},"en",[124,128,129,130,127,131,132,133,134,135,136,137,138,139,140,141,142,143,144,145,146,147,148,149,150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,126,163,125,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184],"zh",[123,124,125,126,127],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools-research","generative-api-boundaries","generation-delivery-contracts","asset-validation-contracts","asset-selection-feedback","visual-evidence-research","visual-feedback-mechanisms","game-development-evaluation","benchmark-reproducibility","gameplay-state-contracts","agent-interface-evidence","catalog-review-coverage","source-revision-notes","community-case-research","overview","catalog","contributing","media-sources","icon-sources","content-m